  "body": "Recently the streams spec added the ability to transfer all streams. This makes it convenient to send those types to a worker without going awkwardly through a message channel.\r\n\r\nI would like to propose a similar addition, and that is the ability to send the `resolve` and `reject` handlers through a `MessageChannel`. This would allow workers to be able to resolve/reject promises on the other thread without having to go through a manual `MessageChannel`.\r\n\r\nAs an example of using this, we can write a request-response API very cleanly:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nconst worker = new Worker(\"./plot.js\");\r\n\r\nasync function drawSprite(angle) {\r\n    const imageData = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\r\n        worker.postMessage({ angle, resolve, reject }, [resolve, reject]);\r\n    });\r\n    ctx.putImage(imageData, 0, 0);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n```js\r\n// plot.js\r\n\r\n// ...\r\n\r\nself.addEventListener(\"message\", event => {\r\n    const imageData = new ImageData(SPRITE_WIDTH, SPRITE_HEIGHT);\r\n\r\n    const { angle, resolve } = event.data;\r\n    // draw sprite with angle\r\n    resolve(imageData);\r\n});\r\n```",
